thor_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 4.4.1 Stable\n\n### System information\n\nWin11 - Godot 4.4.1 stable \n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen creating custom resources, using the ```@export``` attribute with any Node-derived class will give an error. When you export only built-in types and/or ```Variant```, the error does not appear. The error messaging states that the cause of the error is the inheritance. If that is the case then the error should occur when any type is exported, including built-ins.\n\nThe error:\n```\nParse Error: Node export is only supported in Node-derived classes, but the current class inherits \"Resource\".\n```\n\nI believe either the error messaging needs to be updated to clarify what is the cause of the error. Or the error parsing needs to be updated to error out if exporting built-ins is a bug.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a custom resource class and ```export``` any built-in and the error will not appear.\n\n\nThe following will cause an error:\n```gdscript\nclass_name MyResource extends Resource\n\n@export var my_dict : Dictionary[MyType, String]\n```\n\nBut this will not\n```gdscript\nclass_name MyResource extends Resource\n\n@export var my_dict : Dictionary[String, String]\n```\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MVP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20258748/MVP.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"The-Bush","id":35176305,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTc2MzA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35176305?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Bush","html_url":"https://github.com/The-Bush","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Bush/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Bush/fo